Bring the Ottawa pages up to the Spacefully LP practices; first-party photos

The scaffold hotlinked the client's WordPress media library, and tcccanada.com
has since been rebuilt on a new theme: all 29 of those URLs, logo included,
return 404, so every photo on every track was broken. 27 of the 29 files were
recovered from the Internet Archive - the scaffold's exact choices - and the
two that were never archived were replaced with the client's own files
(Laurier: the one surviving Laurier upload, an exterior; the Queensway mosaic
slot: the day office already used on Meeting Rooms). A contact sheet of all
21 photos was checked against their alt text; four location-card alts that
said "Workspace" over a kitchen, lounges and now an exterior describe the
frame instead.

Photography pipeline (npm run images), after the HighQ and MYVO ones: WebP at
each role's widths with srcset and intrinsic sizes, 1200x630 OG cards per
track, favicons from the current brand mark, and - new here - it WRITES
src/lib/pics.ts and each shell's hero preload from the files it produced, so
neither can drift the way HighQ's hand-kept copy did. Sources stay outside
the repo in ../tcc_images. Phones now get 400-700px heroes instead of 2560px
JPEGs.

Carried over from the other LPs:
- PostHog, proxied first-party through /ph (rules above the catch-alls)
- analytics push also calls gtag() when present: GA4 ignores bare dataLayer
  pushes on a gtag page (HighQ)
- links to #quote or any section work from outside (scrollToHash; MYVO still
  lands them at the top)
- body overflow-x: clip, FAQ overflow-anchor: none (HighQ's FAQ scroll bugs)
- npm run preview (:4301, analytics stripped, GTM too, form posts logged not
  sent) and npm run snapshot for before/after review
- build guard: scripts/check-forms.mjs fails the build when a page posts a
  field its Netlify stub lacks, instead of Netlify dropping it silently

Verified on the built pages at 1440 and 390px: 0 broken images, 0 requests to
tcccanada.com, 0 horizontal overflow, analytics absent in preview.

